#  Java Loops (For, While, Do-While)

##  What is a Loop?

A loop is used to **repeat a block of code multiple times** instead of writing the same code again.


## 1. For Loop

###  When to Use

Use a **for loop** when you know **exactly how many times** you want to repeat an action.


### Syntax

```java
for (initialization; condition; increment) {
    // code to run
}
```


### Example

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    System.out.println("Hello");
}
```


###  Explanation

* `int i = 1` → starting point
* `i <= 5` → condition to continue
* `i++` → increases by 1 each time


###  Output

```
Hello
Hello
Hello
Hello
Hello
```


##  2. While Loop

###  When to Use

Use a **while loop** when you don’t know how many times to repeat, but you have a **condition**.


###  Syntax

```java
while (condition) {
    // code to run
}
```


###  Example

```java
int i = 1;

while (i <= 5) {
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;
}
```


###  Explanation

* The loop runs **as long as the condition is true**
* You must update the variable (`i++`) to avoid infinite loop


###  Important

If you forget `i++` → ❌ the loop will run forever


 3. Do-While Loop

###  When to Use

Use a **do-while loop** when you want the code to run **at least once**, even if the condition is false.



### Syntax

```java
do {
    // code to run
} while (condition);
```


### Example

```java
int i = 1;

do {
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;
} while (i <= 5);
```


###  Key Difference

* Runs **first**, checks condition later


### ⚡ Example (Runs Once Even If False)

```java
int i = 10;

do {
    System.out.println("Runs once");
} while (i < 5);
```


##  Comparison

| Loop Type  | When to Use                            |
| ---------- | -------------------------------------- |
| For Loop   | When number of repetitions is known    |
| While Loop | When repetition depends on a condition |
| Do-While   | When code must run at least once       |


##  Key Takeaways

* Loops help reduce repetition
* Always define a condition
* Always update your variable
* Avoid infinite loops

